<title>HONG KONG: Hsin Chong jumps on stake sale rumours.</title>
<headline>Hsin Chong jumps on stake sale rumours.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Hsin Chong Construction Group Ltd rose on buying fueled by rumours that a Chinese interest was considering taking a stake in the company, brokers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Rumours that a Chinses party is interested in taking a stake in the company has fueled anticipation of future asset injection and better growth prospects with Chinese participation,&quot; said a sales manager at local brokerage.</p>
<p>Hsin Chong officials were not immediately available for comment. The company shares rose HK$0.79 or 54.11 percent to HK$2.25 in mid-morning on volume of 38.83 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370.  http://www.hk97.com</p>
